WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.935
Hello and welcome. I'm James Murphy.

00:00:02.935 --> 00:00:08.913
In this&nbsp;video, we're talking about multiple assignments or chained assignments in Python.

00:00:08.913 --> 00:00:12.191
These multiple&nbsp;assignments are different than tuple assignments.

00:00:12.191 --> 00:00:14.747
Multiple assignments involve multiple equal signs

00:00:14.747 --> 00:00:17.970
not multiple things on the side of the equal sign.

00:00:17.970 --> 00:00:19.950
But they can be combined.

00:00:19.950 --> 00:00:24.000
By the end of this video,&nbsp;I hope that you're going to understand multiple assignments well enough

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:28.902
that you can understand&nbsp;something like this extremely tricky example.

00:00:28.902 --> 00:00:33.520
But before I get into the explanations of&nbsp;things, let's talk about this video's sponsor.

